%U A402368 124678051,124684356,124684611,145189316,149274501,150563492,150888581,150947556,150953861,150954116,160286916,161575907,161900996,161959971
%N A402368 Numbers that are the sum of eight distinct positive 8th powers.
%e A402368 a(1) = Sum_{k=1..8} k^8 = A031971(8) is clearly the smallest such number.
%e A402368 a(2) = Sum_{k=1..7} k^8 + 9^8 is the next larger such number, then
%e A402368 a(3) = Sum_{k=1..9} k^8 - 7^8 (i.e., 7^8 is omitted in the sum)
%e A402368 a(4) = Sum_{k=1..9} k^8 - 6^8 (i.e., 6^8 is omitted in the sum)
%e A402368 a(5) = Sum_{k=1..9} k^8 - 5^8 (i.e., 5^8 is omitted in the sum)
%e A402368 a(6) = Sum_{k=1..9} k^8 - 4^8 (i.e., 4^8 is omitted in the sum)
%e A402368 a(7) = Sum_{k=1..9} k^8 - 3^8 (i.e., 3^8 is omitted in the sum)
%e A402368 a(8) = Sum_{k=1..9} k^8 - 2^8 (i.e., 2^8 is omitted in the sum)
%e A402368 a(9) = Sum_{k=2..9} k^8.
%e A402368 We see that the first 9 terms are a(n) = a(9)+1 - (10-n)^8, 1 <= n <= 9.
%e A402368 Then the sequence goes on with 2 omitted terms among {k^8, 1 <= k <= 10}, then with 3 omitted terms among {k^8, 1 <= k <= 11}, etc. This pattern breaks when m^8 < Sum_{k=m-8..m-1} k^8, which happens for m = 13.
%o A402368 (PARI) A402368_first(n=50, k=8)=my(L=List(),m=k); while(#L<n^1.05, forvec(v=vector(k,i,[m^(i==k),m]), listput(L,sum(i=1,k,v[i]^k)), 2); m++); Set(L)[1..n]
%Y A402368 Cf. A001016 (eighth powers), A031971 (Sum k^n, k=1..n).
%Y A402368 Row 8 of A402364 (n-th row lists sums of n distinct n-th powers > 0).
%Y A402368 Cf. A004431 (sums of two distinct squares > 0), A024975 (sums of 3 distinct cubes > 0), A176197 (sums of 4 distinct 4th powers > 0), A402365 (sums of 5 distinct 5th powers > 0), A402366 (sums of 6 distinct 6th powers > 0), A402367 (sums of 7 distinct 7th powers > 0), ...
